2615941", "image_digest": null, "last_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": null, "model_max_tokens": null, "output_tail": "[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nDelegating the search/members investigation to a subagent while I handle the rest.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: task]\n[tool: todowrite]\n[tool: bash]\nApplying all fixes.\n[tool: bash]\n[tool: todowrite]\nAll tests now pass: `python3 -m unittest` ran 16 tests with no failures. The first run showed only 15 because `test_search.py` couldn't be imported. I only changed code in `catalog/` and left the tests alone. A subagent looked into `test_search.py` and `test_members.py`, and I checked what it found before making those changes.\n\nFixes:\n- **`catalog/search.py`**: the import pointed to a module that doesn't exist, `catalog.nonexistent`. It now imports `normalize` from `catalog.text`.\n- **`catalog/members.py`**: the borrowing limit was 3, but the comment and the tests both say 5. Changed `MAX_BORROWED` to 5.\n- **`catalog/books.py`**: `parse_book` kept the year as a string. It now converts it to a number with `int(year)`.\n- **`catalog/fees.py`**: the fee was the number of days late *plus* 0.25. It is now days late *times* 0.25.\n- **`catalog/inventory.py`**: `recent(n)` returned one event too many. It now uses `self._history[-n:]` and returns an empty list when `n` is 0 or less. I added that guard because `[-0:]` would return the whole history.\n- **`catalog/factory.py`**: added the missing third sample book, `Book(\"Emma\", \"Austen\", 1815, 1)`. The tests only check the title, so I picked the author, year and copy count myself.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "params_stripped": [], "params_stripped_requests": 0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 0, "replies_ok": null, "replies_throttled": null, "requests_cache_read": 67885, "requests_cache_write": 53394, "requests_cost_usd": 0.342703, "requests_count": 10, "requests_input